 "comment": "WP-4.2 soak (PLAN_v4 section 5 Phase 4 row 4.2): two in-game days of the owner's testWorld (tests/golden/save/testworld/world: level.dat and region/r.0.-1.mcr), opened with the loading constructor through a temp copy (\"world\": \"load\", as tick/testworld-6000) that autosaves every 40 ticks; chunks missing from the save are generated (seed 123 from level.dat) and populated. The player gets id 9: the saved entities of the preloaded chunks join first and take 0-8 (an item, zombies, skeletons, a spider and creepers, which die at difficulty 0, EntityMob.java:22). It stands on the sand at the spawn point (21.5, 65, -63.5) as in tick/testworld-6000 until t=16000, with a garden site built at (X, Z) = (45, -64) at t=0 inside its random-tick range (no dig or use_item there); from t=16000 it works a site at (296, -296) (in r.0.-1's area but not in the save, so generated), and at t=32000 set_pos puts it back on the spawn sand. A site is a 15 x 9 stone platform at y = 100 (x X-7..X+7, z Z-4..Z+4, the 15 x 12 x 9 box above it cleared to air first, so the site does not depend on the terrain and the scenario runs under check-sensitivity.sh's flipped seed), built with fill/set_block ops at the tick the player arrives: the player at (X-5.5, 101, Z+0.5); a dirt block beside it dug with the stone shovel (8 dig ticks from t+2, broken on the 4th; the drop is picked up), dirt placed back with use_item at t+20 and a torch at t+21; birch, spruce and oak saplings on dirt (random-tick growth, WorldGenForest / WorldGenTaiga2 / WorldGenTrees or BigTree); a farm row (two farmland blocks with crops around a still-water block, cactus on sand and reeds on dirt beside the water); two leaves blocks with the check-decay bit (no log in range: they decay on a random tick and may drop a sapling); sand and gravel in the air (falling-sand entities); a fenced 2 x 2 pen with a pig and a chicken (eggs); a cobblestone item out of the player's reach (despawns at age 6000); outside the platform, three one-block pillars: flowing water at (X+11, 101, Z) and flowing lava at (X, 101, Z-9) pouring down to the terrain (long fluid cascades, lava fires on the ground) and an eternal fire on netherrack at (X+11, 101, Z-4) next to a plank. Moving on, set_pos puts the player on the next site (y = feet + (double) 1.62F, the yOffset, since set_pos is Entity.setPosition) with set_motion 0; a revisited site is not rebuilt. The final block_box over the spawn covers y = 58..71 and the chest at (9, 64, -61). Difficulty 0 with natural spawning on (the reproducible setting, tools/oracle/census.md section 3: animals and squid spawn, hostile spawning stays off). set_weather at t=0 sets thunder_time to 100000000 so no thunderstorm starts during the run: lightning bolts draw from a never-seeded Entity.rand (census section 3) and one striking near an entity would make the oracle irreproducible; rain_time 20000 starts the first rain at t=20000 (level.dat's own rain timer would not run out in this run). Every op position is preloaded before tick 0 (5 x 5 chunks); the player then loads the 19 x 19 chunks around it (random ticks, World.updateBlocksAndPlayCaveSounds) and generates and populates them at each new site; nothing unloads (b1.7.3 has no chunk dropping in single player). Animals left behind more than 128 blocks despawn (EntityLiving.despawnEntity). Dumps (tests/golden/README.md \"Soak\"): rng_state every 100 ticks; the player's entity line every 500; world_time, weather, scheduled_ticks, player_state, inventory, every entity, and the chunk_digest of the 3 x 3 chunks around every site every 1000; at the last tick additionally the rest of each site's 5 x 5 chunks, a block_box over each site and the full scheduled-tick list.",
